# Test: inferred [do] monad from return annotation (Rule 1) — function definition form.
# [[fn@[ok: Int  err: Str] [] [do ...]]] stores the anonymous function at auto-index 0.
# The function body uses [do ...] with ok+err annotation → monad resolved to "result"
# at typecheck time (Rule 1). The program DEFINES the function but does not CALL it,
# so the output is Dict({0: Function()}).
# To observe the do-body execution, call the function: [fn [] [do ...]] applied to [].
[[fn@[ok: Int  err: Str] []
  [do [x: [Ok 42]] [Ok x]]]]
=== out
Dict({0: Function()})
